# Every setting below is commented out ON PURPOSE.
#
# The deploy (deploy/aws/ci-deploy.sh) copies this file to deploy/aws/.env on any host that has
# none. An active line here would then become real configuration on that host:
# APP_ENV=zs-sandbox would point dev at the sandbox secrets, and the example.com
# URLs would break login and CORS. Commented out, the copy sets nothing, and
# deploy/aws/ec2/deploy-component.sh treats a deploy/aws/.env with no settings as absent,
# so the host falls back to the repo's .env.defaults.
#
# To configure a host by hand (sandbox / prod), copy this to deploy/aws/.env and
# uncomment what you need.

# NerveCenter deployment environment. Copy to deploy/aws/.env on the EC2 host.
#
# NerveCenter shares AWS Secrets Manager, the S3 bucket and the Postgres RDS with the
# dataverse (ai4dm) suite. Canonical keys (db_host, s3_bucket, AZURE_*) match the dataverse
# convention so the same secret set can feed both apps. NerveCenter-only values use NC_.
#
# Systems the agent works with (Databricks, Jira, ServiceNow, Snowflake, Git knowledge
# repositories, extra MCP servers) are configured in the app under Connectors and Knowledge.
# Their secrets go to AWS Secrets Manager; operations.yaml only holds ${VAR} references.

# ---- Environment + AWS ------------------------------------------------------
# APP_ENV=zs-sandbox
# BEACON_ENV drives Secrets Manager path selection (beacon/<env>/<group>).
# MUST be set on the pod host or hydration falls back to beacon/development/*
# which does not exist for sandbox/dev/prod — same rule as ai4dm / ai_for_data.
# BEACON_ENV=zs-sandbox
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
# USE_AWS_SECRETS=true
# AWS_SECRET_PREFIX=beacon
# AWS_SECRET_GROUPS=nervecenter,common

# ---- AWS credentials (IRSA on EKS / instance role on EC2) ------------------
# On EKS the ServiceAccount must be annotated with eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn
# so the mutating webhook injects AWS_ROLE_ARN + AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE
# into the pod. Compose now forwards those into the container. If IRSA is not
# available (bare EC2, local run), set static creds or irsa_iam_role_arn here:
# AWS_ROLE_ARN=
# irsa_iam_role_arn=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# NerveCenter-scoped secret prefix override. Leave blank to reuse AWS_SECRET_PREFIX above.
# NC_SECRET_PREFIX=

# ---- Public URL routing -----------------------------------------------------
# /apps/nervecenter for sandbox, /nervecenter for dev. Must match the ALB/ingress path.
# PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/apps/nervecenter
# FRONTEND_PORT=8420
# BACKEND_PORT=8421
# OPS_PUBLIC_URL=https://nervecenter.example.com/apps/nervecenter
# Exact browser origin. Wildcard CORS is rejected in production.
# OPS_CORS_ORIGIN=https://nervecenter.example.com

# ---- Shared dataverse Postgres RDS (tickets, tasks, inbox) -------------------
# Set NC_DATABASE_URL, or the discrete db_* keys. When sharing a database with a sibling app,
# set NC_DB_SCHEMA so NerveCenter's ops_* tables live in their own schema.
# NC_DATABASE_URL=
# NC_DB_SCHEMA=nervecenter
# db_host=
# db_port=5432
# db_name=
# db_user=
# db_password=
# OPS_METADATA_STORE=postgres

# ---- Shared dataverse S3 bucket (agent workspace mirror) --------------------
# The workspace (operations.yaml, knowledge/, workflows/, custom skills, task files) is restored
# from s3://<bucket>/<prefix>/workspace/ on boot and pushed back every OPS_WORKSPACE_SYNC_SECONDS.
# s3_bucket=
# s3_bucket_arn=
# NC_S3_PREFIX=nervecenter
# OPS_WORKSPACE_SYNC_SECONDS=60

# ---- Identity ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Centralized Azure SSO is the default. The backend forwards the browser cookie to
# OPS_SSO_SESSION_URL and trusts only the user that service returns.
# OPS_IDENTITY_MODE=central-sso
# OPS_SSO_SESSION_URL=https://shared-auth.example.com/dataverse/apps/api/v1/auth/session
# VITE_AZURE_SSO_ENABLED=true
# VITE_AUTH_ENABLED=true
# VITE_AUTH_API_BASE_URL=/dataverse/apps/api/v1
# Shared credential between the nginx frontend and the backend. The EC2 deploy script replaces
# an absent or placeholder value with a persistent random one.
# OPS_TRUSTED_IDENTITY_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-gateway-secret
# OPS_INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# OPS_DEFAULT_USER_ID=demo.user
# OPS_DEFAULT_USER_NAME=Demo User
# Comma-separated user ids that are admins from the first sign-in. Others start as developers.
# OPS_ADMIN_USER_IDS=

# ---- Agent ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comes from beacon/<env>/common in Secrets Manager when USE_AWS_SECRETS is on.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# NC_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Model for agent sessions (blank = the SDK default). How many tasks run at once.
# OPS_AGENT_MODEL=
# OPS_MAX_CONCURRENT_TASKS=3
# OPS_MAX_TURNS_PER_RUN=
# Ticket poller (imports in-scope tickets and starts triage tasks per Settings > Ticketing) and
# routine scheduler. Set to 0 to disable.
# OPS_TICKET_POLLING=1
# OPS_TICKET_POLL_SECONDS=15
# OPS_INTEGRATION_SYNC=1
# OPS_INTEGRATION_SYNC_SECONDS=15
# OPS_KNOWLEDGE_SYNC_SECONDS=15
# OPS_GITHUB_SYNC_SECONDS=15
# Pause external Jira, Databricks, GitHub and knowledge polling after this many seconds
# without a visible browser heartbeat. Set to 0 to keep polling even when nobody is using the app.
# OPS_SYNC_IDLE_SECONDS=90
# OPS_ROUTINES=1
# OPS_TICKET_PREFIX=OPS

# ---- Optional deployment-level platform credentials -------------------------
# The normal path is Connectors in the app. These are honoured when present.
# DATABRICKS_HOST=
# DATABRICKS_TOKEN=
# SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT=
# SNOWFLAKE_USER=
# SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD=
# SNOWFLAKE_PRIVATE_KEY=
# SNOWFLAKE_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSPHRASE=
# SNOWFLAKE_TOKEN=
# SNOWFLAKE_TOKEN_TYPE=PROGRAMMATIC_ACCESS_TOKEN
# SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE=
# SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE=
# SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA=
# SNOWFLAKE_ROLE=
# SERVICENOW_INSTANCE=
# SERVICENOW_USERNAME=
# SERVICENOW_PASSWORD=
# OPS_SERVICENOW_SECRET_REF=integrations/servicenow/credential

# No AWS access key or secret is needed. The SDK uses the EC2 instance role, which needs
# Secrets Manager read/write under the prefix, S3 read/write under <prefix>/workspace/, and
# RDS network access.

# ---- Email (SMTP) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Either save the Email connector in the app or set these five variables; with them set the
# Connectors page shows the mail server as "from environment" and the agent sends through it.
# The relay must be reachable from the host that runs the backend (Connectors > Email > Test
# proves it). Plain SMTP on 25 when SMTP_USE_TLS=false; STARTTLS when true.
# EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=true
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=smtp
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=25
# SMTP_USE_TLS=false

# Frontend build setting: page Refresh countdown in seconds; 0 disables. Rebuild the frontend.
VITE_AUTO_REFRESH_SECONDS=300
